# Bump release version for main

The site header shows `v{RELEASE_VERSION}` and links to `/releases/{version}`. Both come from [apps/web/src/lib/release.ts](apps/web/src/lib/release.ts). The number and its comments must change on **every merge to `main`**.

## When to bump

If the change will be committed, opened as a PR, or merged to `main`, bump the version **in the same change**. Do this even for docs-only or CSS-only work.

Skip only when the working tree has no changes (nothing to merge).

## How

1. Read `RELEASES` (newest first) in `apps/web/src/lib/release.ts`.
2. Bump **patch** (`0.2.0` → `0.2.1`) for the usual slice (fixes, docs, UI, one scenario).
3. Bump **minor** (`0.2.1` → `0.3.0`) when adding a new scenario category or a visitor-facing product area.
4. **Prepend** a new `{ version, date, title, notes }` object. `notes` are the visitor-facing comments (what changed and why). `RELEASE_VERSION` is `RELEASES[0].version`.
5. Set the same version string on root [`package.json`](package.json) and [`apps/web/package.json`](apps/web/package.json).
6. Do not invent a second changelog file.

```text
# ❌ BAD — PR to main, RELEASES[0] still the previous version
# ✅ GOOD — same PR prepends 0.2.1 with comments and matches both package.json versions
```
